# MODELLER PLAYGROUND — the Modeller's OWN building set on GH, FULLY ISOLATED from the viewer (zero OCI).
# The viewer is never touched (it keeps fetching viewer/buildings → OCI). Only the modeller reads modeller/.
#   • Small SINGLE-file buildings (<100MB): regular git blobs, served directly by GH Pages (Range + gzip).
#   • Terminal: split. meta.db (19MB bbox WALK substrate) = regular blob; geo.db (250MB meshes) = Git LFS
#     (.gitattributes), so it clears git's 100MB push limit. NOTE GH PAGES serves the LFS POINTER, not the
#     bytes — the mesh content is fetched from the LFS media endpoint (raw/media.githubusercontent.com),
#     verified live post-merge. The WALK needs only meta (a regular blob), so the walker is unaffected either way.
!modeller/SampleHouse_extracted.db
!modeller/Duplex_extracted.db
!modeller/SampleCastle_extracted.db
!modeller/SampleCastle_ARC_extracted.db
!modeller/Terminal_meta.db
!modeller/Terminal_geo.db
!modeller/terminal_rules.db
!modeller/mep_rw.db
!modeller/Ifc4_Revit_extracted.db
*.bin
# Exception: small, permanent, hand-vendored staffage prop asset (32KB, real geometry extracted
# from BimWhale_Advanced — see viewer/textures/staffage/props/NOTICE.txt) — NOT a regenerated
# per-building positions/geometry cache like the rest of *.bin, same tracked-asset standing as the
# PNG cutouts it sits next to.
!viewer/textures/staffage/props/*.bin
